WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:08.367
In this walkthrough we'll see how
access is governed, and why you can see
what you can see, in the OpenTRMS Workbench.

2
00:00:08.367 --> 00:00:18.000
The first walkthrough said that what you can see
depends on your entitlements. The Access Policy
Console is where those entitlements are actually defined.

3
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:29.433
Functional groups come first. A functional group is a
bundle of permissions — the scopes column lists exactly
what the group allows, which is what makes it auditable.

4
00:00:29.433 --> 00:00:39.067
Data groups answer the other half of the
question. Not what you may do, but which
books, portfolios and counterparties you may do it to.

5
00:00:39.067 --> 00:00:49.667
Grants are where the two meet a person. A grant
ties a user to a group, and this is the record
that explains why an individual has the access they have.

6
00:00:49.667 --> 00:01:03.067
Segregation of duties is checked here too. Some combinations are
not allowed together — booking a trade and approving it, for
instance — and conflicts are surfaced rather than silently permitted.

7
00:01:03.067 --> 00:01:13.767
And recertification closes the loop. Access is
reviewed periodically rather than granted once
and forgotten, which is what auditors will ask to see.

8
00:01:13.767 --> 00:01:21.967
That completes Entitlements and Policy. Every
surface shown here can also be opened from the
agent panel on the right, by asking for it in plain English.
